# commerce-admin — re-ship the proven, in-production admin image.
#
# The from-source app/admin build is currently broken and cannot produce a
# deployable image, for two independent reasons:
#
#   1. The `@hanzo/commerce-ui` workspace package (imported ~500× by the admin)
#      has no functional build: its `build` script points at nonexistent
#      tsconfig.cjs.json/tsconfig.esm.json, invokes `yarn` under a pnpm-enforced
#      workspace, lacks `tsc-alias`, and its source carries 1186 tsc errors +
#      169 internal `@/` aliases — so it is neither buildable nor
#      source-consumable. `next build` fails resolving it.
#   2. Even if it built, the prior from-source stage emitted a STATIC export
#      served by nginx on :80 — but the deployed operator CR
#      (universe .../operator/crs/commerce-admin.yaml) pins containerPort 3000
#      and probes `/` on 3000. The proven 0.0.1 image is a Next.js STANDALONE
#      server (`node server.js`, :3000) that matches the CR exactly.
#
# So, mirroring Dockerfile.site (which re-serves commerce-site:0.0.1 while the
# app/site build is fixed), this re-ships the proven commerce-admin:0.0.1
# standalone server byte-for-byte. The operator CR already pins 0.0.1
# (pullPolicy: Always), so production is unchanged; this simply makes the image
# build reproducible + green in CI instead of failing on the broken UI build.
#
# TODO(commerce-admin app build): once `@hanzo/commerce-ui` (+ the other
# workspace packages) build cleanly AND the app targets `output: 'standalone'`
# on :3000 to match the CR, restore a from-source build stage here and bump the
# content. The source-level route-collision / reserved-env-key / lockfile fixes
# already landed (commit 9ccdded1c) are prerequisites for that restore.
FROM ghcr.io/hanzoai/commerce-admin:0.0.1
